                                "example_id": "bf1ca700-32bd-4648-a250-eef8b2a0bbb2",
                                "sense_id": "c858f280-1d93-3bc2-986b-2e647fa641e0",
                                "text": "Orthid soils are used for grazing or are irrigated for crop production if water is available."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "45e3c1b6-6cc2-4fb5-a5e0-b2ad2ec87bac",
                                "sense_id": "c858f280-1d93-3bc2-986b-2e647fa641e0",
                                "text": "—orthid, great group with a horizon with an accumulation of salts more soluble than gypsum."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f25ee6a2-d753-4a06-b8cd-095f7509a4fa",
                                "sense_id": "c858f280-1d93-3bc2-986b-2e647fa641e0",
                                "text": "When drained, they are comparable in sensitivity to orthid luvisols in an A horizon with a very low clay content."
